{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Come, let us descend.</b> He consulted His court — from His exceeding humility." "<b>Come.</b> Measure for measure — they said ״הָבָה נִבְנֶה״, and He, corresponding to them, took measure and said ״הָבָה נֵרְדָה״." "<b>And let us confound.</b> וּנְבַלְבֵּל; the nun serves in the plural, and the final heh is superfluous — like the heh of נֵרְדָה." "<b>They will not understand.</b> This one asks for a brick and that one brings clay, and this one stands on it and splits his brain."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:18.721527080Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}